Description: Read malformed open tags as the HTML tokenizer does, reporting each
 A quote or "<" in an attribute name is part of the name and reports
 "unexpected-character-in-attribute-name"; upstream threw on "<". A quote
 or "<" in an unquoted value is part of the value and reports
 "unexpected-character-in-unquoted-attribute-value", unless a Twig tag was
 read earlier in that value, where the template decides the quoting. A "/"
 not followed by ">" reports "unexpected-solidus-in-tag" and is ignored, so
 the attributes after it are read; upstream took them into the open tag
 end.
Author: Numiko
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
Test: test/parser/diagnostics.test.ts ("unexpected-character-in-attribute-name", "unexpected-character-in-unquoted-attribute-value", "unexpected-solidus-in-tag")
Last-Update: 2026-11-04
